drm/rockchip: demote the no-splash "failed to parse loader memory" warn.

When U-Boot passes no splash framebuffer (e.g. display disabled or
vidconsole not in stdout), init_loader_memory() fails and the driver
warns "failed to parse loader memory" every boot. That is a normal
configuration, not an error — log it at debug level.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c	2026-07-26 13:21:39
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/rockchip_drm_logo.c	2026-07-26 13:21:39
@@ -1058,7 +1058,7 @@
 	}
 
 	if (init_loader_memory(drm_dev)) {
-		dev_warn(drm_dev->dev, "failed to parse loader memory\n");
+		dev_dbg(drm_dev->dev, "failed to parse loader memory\n");
 		return;
 	}
 
